        },
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\left(\\dfrac a2,\\dfrac a2\\right)$ and $\\left(-\\dfrac a2,-\\dfrac a2\\right)$. The signs match; when $a=0$, both points coincide at $(0,0)$.",
          "worked": "Plot both equations in DESMOS and vary $a$. The two intersections lie on $y=x$ and appear to be $\\left(\\dfrac a2,\\dfrac a2\\right)$ and $\\left(-\\dfrac a2,-\\dfrac a2\\right)$. Changing $a$ to $-a$ leaves both curves unchanged. At $a=0$, the only intersection is $(0,0)$.\nThe example sketch shows $a=2$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": [
            {
              "id": "p53-q13-c-solution-graph",
              "role": "solution",
              "format": "tikz",
              "code": "% mathsmap-diagram-colours {\"version\":1,\"kind\":\"graph\",\"base\":[],\"semantic\":[{\"name\":\"circleBlue\",\"hex\":\"268CFF\",\"reason\":\"circle series\"},{\"name\":\"hyperbolaRed\",\"hex\":\"EF6068\",\"reason\":\"hyperbola series\"}],\"reference\":\"source page 53 p53-q13-c-solution-graph\"}\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.85cm,y=0.85cm]\n\\special{dvisvgm:raw <metadata data-graph-strokes=\"1\"/>}\n\\definecolor{circleBlue}{HTML}{268CFF}\n\\definecolor{hyperbolaRed}{HTML}{EF6068}\n\\path[use as bounding box] (-3.5,-3.2) rectangle (3.5,4.1);\n\\draw[<->,line width=0.5pt] (-3,0)--(3,0) node[right] {$x$};\n\\draw[<->,line width=0.5pt] (0,-3)--(0,3) node[above] {$y$};\n\\draw[circleBlue,line width=0.8pt] (0,0) circle[radius=1.41421356];\n\\draw[hyperbolaRed,line width=0.8pt,<->,domain=0.34:3,samples=100,smooth] plot (\\x,{1/\\x});\n\\draw[hyperbolaRed,line width=0.8pt,<->,domain=-3:-0.34,samples=100,smooth] plot (\\x,{1/\\x});\n\\fill[black] (1,1) circle[radius=1.5pt];\n\\fill[black] (-1,-1) circle[radius=1.5pt];\n\\node[above right] at (1,1) {$(1,1)$};\n\\node[below left] at (-1,-1) {$(-1,-1)$};\n\\node[above left] at (-2,2.8) {$a=2$};\n\\node[circleBlue,right] at (1.6,-1.8) {$x^2+y^2=2$};\n\\node[hyperbolaRed,above right] at (2.7,0.4) {$xy=1$};\n\\end{tikzpicture}",
              "src": null,
              "widthMm": 70,
              "alt": "Mathematical diagram",
              "overlayOf": null,
              "transparent": false,
              "axes": null,
              "spec": {
                "sourcePage": 53,
                "sourceRegion": "Question 13c",
                "description": "Authored common-axis example for a=2, showing the circle and both hyperbola branches, with matching-sign intersection coordinates.",
                "mathematics": "For a=2: x^2+y^2=2 and xy=1. Intersections are (1,1) and (-1,-1). The circle and hyperbola are tangent at both intersections.",
                "answerVisibility": "Answer-only graph; no source graph was supplied."
              },
              "derived": false,
              "reviewStatus": "needs-review"
            }
